Incoming! Get out of there!

17
00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.350
Everyone down!

18
00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.102
(explosion)

19
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.980
(heavy breathing)

20
00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:07.526
My name is Rachel Wild.

21
00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:10.445
I'm a particular
type of lawyer.

22
00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:11.863
(explosion)

23
00:01:12.656 --> 00:01:15.909
My job is to dog and chase down
those who hide their debts

24
00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:18.745
through legal loopholes
and shell companies.

25
00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.789
(explosion)
(grunting)

26
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.793
I work between the moral
and the immoral.

27
00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:26.211
(explosion)

28
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.465
The legal and the illegal.
(gasping)

29
00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:32.926
The black and the white.

30
00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:36.888
I operate in the grey.

31
00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:38.807
(dramatic music)

32
00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:41.893
(phone ringing)

33
00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.400
(phone picked up. distortion)

34
00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:50.444
-BOBBY: Hello?
-Hey. Bobby. I've got some news.

35
00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.946
-Braxton?
-Hey. are you there. Bobby?

36
00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:55.866
No. I'm losing you.
(beeps. call cut off)

37
00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.869
RACHEL: The man on the phone
taught me everything I know.

38
00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.038
Hey. driver. can you find me
a signal?

39
00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:01.997
DRIVER: Of course.

40
00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.041
(engine humming)

41
00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.341
Do you wanna go. er.
stretch your legs?

42
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.301
Okay.

43
00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.014
(phone ringing)

44
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.849
Shall I give you a minute. boss?

45
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:22.434
Thank you. John.

46
00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:24.102
(phone ringing)

47
00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:28.148
(whistling)

48
00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:30.692
Bobby. are you there?

49
00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:33.236
-Braxton. what you got?
-I got a meeting.

50
00:02:33.737 --> 00:02:35.697
-With who?
-Salazar.

51
00:02:36.448 --> 00:02:37.574
You got a meeting
with Salazar?

52
00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:38.784
That's not all I got.

53
00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:40.577
Where's this going. Braxton?

54
00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:42.913
BRAXTON: Where would
you like this to go. hm?

55
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:44.748
BOBBY: Don't tease me.

56
00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.752
-How much?
-Full debt plus interest.

57
00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:53.173
That's impossible.
I don't believe you.

58
00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:55.133
Well. I got the leverage.
I got the agreement.

59
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.052
I got the paperwork
and I got the signature.

60
00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:59.221
-After this. I owe you nothing.
-BRAXTON: Uh-huh.

61
00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.223
-We're done.
-Yeah.

62
00:03:01.682 --> 00:03:03.725
Olsson will take you back
to your hotel.

63
00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:08.730
BOBBY: How do you do it?
Braxton. if you pull this off.

64
00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:11.108
(gun clicks)
you get the full 5%.

65
00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:14.820
-Where are you?
-I'm on Salazar's island.

66
00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:17.531
-I'll be in New York tonight.
-No trouble?

67
00:03:17.781 --> 00:03:19.825
BRAXTON: Nah. I got John
with me for security.

68
00:03:20.492 --> 00:03:23.161
You're on his island and you
only have one man for security?

69
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.247
You just let me worry
about that.

70
00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.958
(gunshot)
Show you up... Oh. Jesus!

71
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.335
-Braxton?
-Fuck! Fuck...

72
00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:32.212
(menacing music)
(whistling)

73
00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:34.673
(alarm beeps. doors lock)
What's happening?

74
00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:36.466
Can you hear me?

75
00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:39.010
(alarm beeps. doors lock)
Braxton. what's happening?

76
00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:41.346
(alarm beeps.
doors lock and unlock)

77
00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:43.557
(whistling)
(doors locking and unlocking)

78
00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:45.016
Braxton. are you there?

79
00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:47.769
(Braxton panicking)
Can you hear me?

80
00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:50.147
(menacing music)
(whistling)

81
00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:54.526
(gunshot)

82
00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:56.570
(alarm beeps. doors unlock)

83
00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:02.784
RACHEL: The upside of this job
is that when you win.

84
00:04:03.785 --> 00:04:04.911
you win big.

85
00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:08.248
The downside is that
when you lose.

86
00:04:09.624 --> 00:04:11.293
you end up in a hole
in the ground.

87
00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:12.753
(gunshot)

88
00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:19.718
(rustling)

89
00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:23.096
Mr Salazar.
contract is void.

90
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.141
Good! If Spencer Goldstein
think they're getting

91
00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:29.436
their billion dollars back.
they can go fuck themselves.

92
00:04:30.395 --> 00:04:34.149
And if they send anyone else
to try. we'll take care of them.

93
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:36.026
(sinister music)

94
00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:36.777
(sinister music)

95
00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:40.155
RACHEL: My clients
are asset managers.

96
00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:42.824
basically sophisticated
bankers.

97
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:45.535
They make money
by loaning money

98
00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:46.953
and when they make mistakes.

99
00:04:47.037 --> 00:04:49.289
they subcontract to people
like Braxton.

100
00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:51.166
Or people like me.

101
00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:53.543
If the first mouse gets sloppy.

102
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.046
then it's the second mouse
that gets the cheese.

103
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.006
(ball pinging)
SECRETARY: Wait. Miss Wild!

104
00:04:58.465 --> 00:04:59.716
It's under control.
Mr Goldstein.

105
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.092
SECRETARY: Wait. Miss Wild!
Please!

106
00:05:01.176 --> 00:05:03.845
-You should have called. Bobby.
-Sorry. Miss Sheen.

107
00:05:03.929 --> 00:05:05.013
We scheduled?

108
00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:06.640
Well. given what happened
to Braxton.

109
00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:07.974
I think we are now.

110
00:05:08.183 --> 00:05:10.435
-I don't have time now.
-Oh. yes. Yes. you do.

111
00:05:10.936 --> 00:05:12.187
I'm here to make you money.

112
00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.273
I'll call you back.

113
00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:18.276
Thanks. ladies. Two minutes.

114
00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:20.612
And don't throw any shit
in this direction.

115
00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:25.617
Why didn't you let him know what
he was getting himself into?

116
00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:27.494
Nobody knew what
he was getting into.

117
00:05:27.661 --> 00:05:28.870
-Hm.
-Anyway. what's it got

118
00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:31.122
to do with you?
-I liked Braxton.

119
00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:34.626
But I didn't like the hand
grenade you passed him.

120
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:39.381
Manny Salazar. He's not really
the guy you loan

121
00:05:39.464 --> 00:05:41.633
a billion dollars and expect
to see it back.

122
00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:43.969
-You weren't thorough. Bobby.
-What did I just say

123
00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:46.137
about throwing shit?
-I'm just here to give you

124
00:05:46.221 --> 00:05:47.973
an opportunity
to recover your money.

125
00:05:48.265 --> 00:05:50.642
-You think you can recover it?
-You know I can.

126
00:05:50.976 --> 00:05:52.811
Ooh. but I know
you're too expensive.

127
00:05:52.894 --> 00:05:55.939
Wouldn't Spencer Goldstein
rather see its money back

128
00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.567
and stop putting bodies
in the ground?

129
00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.609
Careful.

130
00:05:59.693 --> 00:06:00.610
You're pretty-ish.

131
00:06:00.694 --> 00:06:02.153
and funny-ish. and clever.

132
00:06:02.237 --> 00:06:03.780
But you're not
that fucking clever.

133
00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:07.200
Hire someone else. you're...
well. repeating the same mistake

134
00:06:07.284 --> 00:06:10.245
you made with Braxton
and getting the same result.

135
00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.999
-On what terms?
-Standard sub-contract.

136
00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:16.751
You get deniability. Spencer
Goldstein's hands stay clean.

137
00:06:16.835 --> 00:06:20.005
And you only pay me
if I recover the full debt.

138
00:06:20.463 --> 00:06:22.382
-How much?
-Twenty percent.

139
00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.926
-I can get this done for five.
-By who?

140
00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:29.598
You get people killed for five
and you're still left short.

141
00:06:29.723 --> 00:06:31.266
You know. I really
don't like you.

142
00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:33.852
You'll save a dollar
to lose a hundred.

143
00:06:33.935 --> 00:06:35.228
You're a fucking nuisance.

144
00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:38.189
Of course
I'm a fucking nuisance.

145
00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:42.569
I can do it for 7.5%.

146
00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:45.113
Ten percent.
And ten million upfront.

147
00:06:45.864 --> 00:06:47.574
I don't trust you. and...

148
00:06:48.366 --> 00:06:50.535
well. you need skin in the game.

149
00:06:50.911 --> 00:06:52.370
(suspenseful music)

150
00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:54.706
I can make that work.

151
00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:58.627
That was easy.

152
00:06:59.794 --> 00:07:01.671
Don't you have
to call your boss first?

153
00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.884
I don't have to call upstairs.

154
00:07:06.384 --> 00:07:07.218
Impressive!

155
00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:11.348
Every time I visit.
you're a floor higher.

156
00:07:11.473 --> 00:07:14.017
You however do need
a bigger office.

157
00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:15.644
Love you. Bobby.

158
00:07:15.727 --> 00:07:17.354
(door opens)
(phone ringing)

159
00:07:17.562 --> 00:07:18.688
Fuck you. Rachel.
(door closes)

160
00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:21.441
(ominous music)
(sirens blaring)

161
00:07:21.816 --> 00:07:23.318
(intercom beeps)

162
00:07:23.401 --> 00:07:27.155
Asset managers. I'm telling you.
they own the lot.

163
00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.408
I have an asset manager
who manages my money.

164
00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:32.535
(mysterious music)

165
00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:35.163
That's because in spite
of what you look like.

166
00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:36.915
you can still think.

167
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:39.167
But only small picture.

168
00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.630
That's why I have a manager
manage my money.

169
00:07:43.713 --> 00:07:44.881
(door buzzes)

170
00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:52.806
What do you think
they do with it?

171
00:07:53.348 --> 00:07:54.766
I know what they do with it.

172
00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:56.726
They make me more money.

173
00:07:56.893 --> 00:07:58.103
They make you
more money because

174
00:07:58.186 --> 00:07:59.521
they fucking own everything.

175
00:07:59.688 --> 00:08:00.939
I'm happy with that.

176
00:08:01.106 --> 00:08:03.066
You wouldn't be if you knew
what they were up to.

177
00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.026
They're out of control.
They run everything.

178
00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.903
The news. the views.

179
00:08:07.821 --> 00:08:08.863
The weapons. the wars.

180
00:08:08.947 --> 00:08:10.240
There's no conspiracy.

181
00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:12.409
This is good for me
and bad for you.

182
00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:13.994
You should jump in.

183
00:08:14.661 --> 00:08:15.704
The water's warm.

184
00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:18.832
RACHEL: I've worked with Sid
and Bronco for so long.

185
00:08:18.915 --> 00:08:21.251
they're the only two I trust
to keep me alive.

186
00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:24.879
Salazar is a chameleon
who hides behind

187
00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:26.965
hundreds of different
pseudonyms.

188
00:08:27.298 --> 00:08:29.467
Last month.
he was called McIntyre.

189
00:08:29.551 --> 00:08:31.469
The month before that.
Rodriguez.

190
00:08:31.678 --> 00:08:34.431
To corner Salazar.
you must attack him legally

191
00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:35.640
and illegally.

192
00:08:35.724 --> 00:08:37.434
Half my team
deals with the former.

193
00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:39.352
the other half. the latter.

194
00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:40.395
Evening all.

195
00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:41.354
Glover.

196
00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:43.690
Gentlemen.

197
00:08:44.566 --> 00:08:45.817
-Ma'am.
-Ma'am.

198
00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:49.029
Bronco heads a team that
specialises in extraction.

199
00:08:49.112 --> 00:08:51.156
intimidation and sabotage.

200
00:08:51.489 --> 00:08:54.284
And Sidney's band specialises
in corruption.

201
00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:56.369
bribery and covert
surveillance.

202
00:08:56.453 --> 00:08:57.746
So. er...

203
00:08:59.831 --> 00:09:01.082
Salazar?

204
00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:05.045
Manny Salazar is rare
and unique.

205
00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:07.589
Braxton uncovered some
of his hidden assets.

206
00:09:07.672 --> 00:09:09.591
Salazar then buried
those assets.

207
00:09:09.674 --> 00:09:10.550
Along with Braxton.

208
00:09:10.842 --> 00:09:12.427
So. how do we squeeze him?

209
00:09:12.969 --> 00:09:15.138
-We bring him to the table.
-How do we do that?

210
00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.432
Pincer movement.

211
00:09:17.515 --> 00:09:19.434
Combination of practical
and procedural.

212
00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:22.729
Sidney. you will be
going to Saudi.

213
00:09:23.146 --> 00:09:24.439
You. Bronco.

214
00:09:24.856 --> 00:09:25.940
you're coming with me.

215
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.236
First. I must meet Salazar's
infamous lawyer.

216
00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.823
I can only do this concealed
in a Trojan horse.

217
00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:37.994
So sorry to have kept
you waiting. Miss Wild.

218
00:09:38.203 --> 00:09:41.372
I do hope my staff
has taken care of you.

219
00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.750
I'm fine. Mr Horowitz.

220
00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:48.922
So. we have had a chance
to look over your proposal.

221
00:09:49.506 --> 00:09:53.635
And I see that you have quite
substantial capital

222
00:09:53.885 --> 00:09:55.386
that you may need help with.

223
00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.180
(dramatic music fades)

224
00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:58.098
(Bronco sniffs)

225
00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:01.392
I'm sorry...

226
00:10:02.018 --> 00:10:03.311
and you are?

227
00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.063
I don't matter.

228
00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:06.356
(car horn beeps)

229
00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:10.693
RACHEL: Yes. indeed.

230
00:10:10.819 --> 00:10:14.364
I'm particularly interested
in Mr Salazar's portfolio.

231
00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:19.661
That is private information.

232
00:10:19.744 --> 00:10:21.538
I'm sorry. Sir. Do you mind?

233
00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:23.164
That's very valuable.

234
00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:25.083
(statue clunks)

235
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.045
Why do I have the feeling there
is another agenda going on here?

236
00:10:29.504 --> 00:10:31.047
-Hm?
-You'd like to hear it?

237
00:10:31.131 --> 00:10:32.924
No. That's another meeting.

238
00:10:33.675 --> 00:10:34.843
We're done here!

239
00:10:35.718 --> 00:10:38.471
(beep) Can you call Gary
into my office. please.

240
00:10:38.555 --> 00:10:40.348
There is a situation here.

241
00:10:40.431 --> 00:10:42.016
I assure you.
you'd like to listen.

242
00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.476
The alternative is...

243
00:10:44.394 --> 00:10:45.687
very expensive.

244
00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.564
Well. I'm not buying
what you're selling.

245
00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:49.482
GARY! GARY!

246
00:10:56.781 --> 00:10:58.575
Mr Horowitz. is there a problem?

247
00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:00.243
Yeah. Get them out
of my office. now.

248
00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:03.496
Ma'am. Sir.
if you'd like to follow...

249
00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.290
Gary. a moment.

250
00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:08.168
There are two versions of how
this narrative plays out.

251
00:11:08.751 --> 00:11:10.837
Version one. Gary waits
patiently and quietly

252
00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.630
by the door for the next
30 seconds

253
00:11:12.714 --> 00:11:14.257
while we conclude our business.

254
00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.177
And then we leave in a calm
