It's over 200.000. Sir.

515
00:22:09.787 --> 00:22:10.996
Having got his attention.

516
00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:12.706
he's going to be looking
at me very dubiously.

517
00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:14.959
So. I'll need to convince him
that I have

518
00:22:15.042 --> 00:22:16.335
no kind of hidden agenda.

519
00:22:16.919 --> 00:22:18.838
Naturally. being the host
and rather paranoid.

520
00:22:18.921 --> 00:22:20.881
he's going to assume that
I'm a grifter and he's the mark.

521
00:22:20.965 --> 00:22:22.508
So. he'll challenge me.

522
00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:24.552
-May I?
-Please.

523
00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:28.180
What do you say.
5.000 a point?

524
00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:30.057
Sure.

525
00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:31.851
(dice rolling)
(suspenseful music)

526
00:22:31.934 --> 00:22:33.018
SID: Using the loaded dice.

527
00:22:33.102 --> 00:22:34.353
I'll continue
my winning streak.

528
00:22:34.979 --> 00:22:36.939
Simultaneously.
I will refuse payment.

529
00:22:37.815 --> 00:22:39.567
He will insist on paying me.

530
00:22:40.067 --> 00:22:41.777
I make a point
of paying my debts.

531
00:22:42.194 --> 00:22:44.071
But here's where
I make my final move.

532
00:22:44.154 --> 00:22:47.199
You can repay me
by giving me a rematch.

533
00:22:47.575 --> 00:22:48.784
but with a gentleman's bet

534
00:22:48.868 --> 00:22:49.785
and only for $10.

535
00:22:50.286 --> 00:22:51.328
RACHEL: You will lose.

536
00:22:51.412 --> 00:22:52.746
And as a token of a payment.

537
00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:54.373
you will offer him a gift.

538
00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:57.960
It just happens that that gift
is a statue he covets.

539
00:22:58.085 --> 00:22:59.753
Open exhibit B.

540
00:23:00.129 --> 00:23:01.964
(clicking. sliding)
(suspenseful music)

541
00:23:02.089 --> 00:23:04.091
In scurries the Trojan rat.

542
00:23:05.509 --> 00:23:07.720
It seems luck has gone my way.

543
00:23:08.012 --> 00:23:09.013
Well played.

544
00:23:09.179 --> 00:23:11.891
Er. rather embarrassingly.

545
00:23:11.974 --> 00:23:13.851
I don't carry that sort of cash.

546
00:23:14.268 --> 00:23:17.062
If you'll allow me. I'll just
pop something in the post?

547
00:23:17.605 --> 00:23:20.065
RACHEL: People are not
suspicious of those that give.

548
00:23:20.149 --> 00:23:21.525
Only those that take.

549
00:23:21.609 --> 00:23:24.945
Sir. a gift has arrived
from Mr Kershner.

550
00:23:25.029 --> 00:23:27.448
Wolfgang's office
is a Faraday cage.

551
00:23:27.531 --> 00:23:30.576
an impenetrable firewall
preventing anyone or anything

552
00:23:30.659 --> 00:23:31.994
from accessing his data.

553
00:23:32.119 --> 00:23:34.747
However. once you're inside
of said cage

554
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:36.624
and within 12 feet
of his computer.

555
00:23:37.041 --> 00:23:38.208
we're in his world.

556
00:23:38.334 --> 00:23:39.793
Our statue is a bug.

557
00:23:39.877 --> 00:23:42.087
a camera
and a tempest attack device.

558
00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:43.881
We can start to put names
to companies

559
00:23:43.964 --> 00:23:45.591
and untangle his financial web.

560
00:23:46.091 --> 00:23:48.677
Bob's your uncle.
Fanny's your aunt. We're in.

561
00:23:48.969 --> 00:23:50.471
Now. I'm inside
Wolfgang's world.

562
00:23:50.554 --> 00:23:52.598
we can start to peel back
the onion.

563
00:23:53.265 --> 00:23:55.434
Once I have the legal traction
to freeze some more

564
00:23:55.517 --> 00:23:56.727
of his hidden assets...

565
00:23:57.061 --> 00:23:59.063
Oh. Wolfgang. I've got you now.

566
00:23:59.188 --> 00:24:01.398
...this will accelerate
a desire to reach a deal.

567
00:24:01.482 --> 00:24:02.900
The court approves
the application

568
00:24:02.983 --> 00:24:05.069
to seek international
attachment orders.

569
00:24:05.152 --> 00:24:06.779
Objection. Your Honour!

570
00:24:06.862 --> 00:24:07.821
Overruled!

571
00:24:07.947 --> 00:24:09.281
(gavel bangs)
Thank you. Your Honour.

572
00:24:12.493 --> 00:24:13.827
She's a monster.
(phone ringing)

573
00:24:13.953 --> 00:24:15.496
However. in order to get

574
00:24:15.579 --> 00:24:17.247
the unpalatable deal
that I want.

575
00:24:17.373 --> 00:24:19.208
I will need to look Salazar
in the eye.

576
00:24:19.291 --> 00:24:20.167
Hello?

577
00:24:20.668 --> 00:24:21.669
Hello?

578
00:24:21.752 --> 00:24:22.753
Oh. Mr Horowitz.

579
00:24:22.836 --> 00:24:24.213
how lovely to hear from you.

580
00:24:24.713 --> 00:24:25.798
Okay. sweetheart.

581
00:24:27.049 --> 00:24:28.801
200. That's it.

582
00:24:28.926 --> 00:24:31.470
Has anyone ever told you
you have a wonderful timbre

583
00:24:31.553 --> 00:24:32.554
to your voice.

584
00:24:33.222 --> 00:24:34.306
I'm trying to place it.

585
00:24:34.807 --> 00:24:35.641
That's funny?

586
00:24:35.891 --> 00:24:36.892
200 is funny.

587
00:24:37.017 --> 00:24:38.477
(snaps fingers)
I got it.

588
00:24:38.769 --> 00:24:41.355
From the 1950s hit
The African Queen

589
00:24:41.438 --> 00:24:44.024
starring Katherine Hepburn
and Humphrey Bogart.

590
00:24:44.149 --> 00:24:46.360
You sound just like
Katherine Hepburn.

591
00:24:46.860 --> 00:24:47.736
Okay.

592
00:24:47.861 --> 00:24:49.238
(water lapping)

593
00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:50.990
300.

594
00:24:51.073 --> 00:24:52.700
I wanna sit down with Salazar.

595
00:24:52.825 --> 00:24:55.160
Since I can't talk to you.
I wanna talk to him.

596
00:24:55.494 --> 00:24:58.539
(dial tone)
What?! You f...You fu...

597
00:24:58.622 --> 00:25:00.958
You fucking cu...

598
00:25:01.166 --> 00:25:02.334
Salam Alaikum.

599
00:25:02.418 --> 00:25:03.752
Salazar doesn't know it yet.

600
00:25:03.836 --> 00:25:05.629
but he's going to agree
to a meeting.

601
00:25:05.838 --> 00:25:07.172
It's gonna happen on the island.

602
00:25:07.506 --> 00:25:09.383
That's the only place
he'll feel safe.

603
00:25:09.466 --> 00:25:12.553
It's just a question of when.
but there's still plenty of time

604
00:25:12.636 --> 00:25:14.430
for you and your boys to put
in the infrastructure

605
00:25:14.513 --> 00:25:15.848
and prepare for the worst.

606
00:25:15.931 --> 00:25:16.724
Bronco?

607
00:25:17.474 --> 00:25:18.809
I'm sure you've had
a sniff around.

608
00:25:19.268 --> 00:25:20.477
How do we feel about that?

609
00:25:20.561 --> 00:25:21.812
I think we feel okay.

610
00:25:22.229 --> 00:25:23.272
Okay.

611
00:25:23.355 --> 00:25:24.356
Better get more boots then.

612
00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:26.483
(dramatic music)

613
00:25:30.362 --> 00:25:31.196
BRONCO: Phase two.

614
00:25:31.488 --> 00:25:32.906
Planning and preparation.

615
00:25:33.323 --> 00:25:35.200
(boat motor humming)

616
00:25:40.080 --> 00:25:41.248
Mr Beauregard.

617
00:25:42.249 --> 00:25:43.834
Buenos días. Captain Sensible.

618
00:25:44.043 --> 00:25:45.044
Love the shirt.

619
00:25:45.335 --> 00:25:46.128
It's silk.

620
00:25:46.962 --> 00:25:47.880
Like my sheets.

621
00:25:48.922 --> 00:25:49.715
Course it is.

622
00:25:49.798 --> 00:25:50.883
RACHEL: My insurance policy

623
00:25:50.966 --> 00:25:52.593
will need to consist
of a full team.

624
00:25:52.676 --> 00:25:53.635
Baker...

625
00:25:53.844 --> 00:25:55.637
Baker will be in charge
of explosives

626
00:25:55.721 --> 00:25:56.680
and munitions.

627
00:25:57.181 --> 00:26:00.100
Moreno is a wheel man in charge
of on-ground transport.

628
00:26:00.851 --> 00:26:04.271
Dunne is in charge of
aviation...and cynicism.

629
00:26:04.563 --> 00:26:05.856
This is Gucci.

630
00:26:05.939 --> 00:26:06.899
He's in charge of tech.

631
00:26:09.985 --> 00:26:11.153
I just told you.

632
00:26:11.236 --> 00:26:12.863
It's silk.
(bag clunks)

633
00:26:13.072 --> 00:26:15.491
Their principal agenda will be
getting me off the island

634
00:26:15.574 --> 00:26:17.367
and should I need
to leave quickly.

635
00:26:17.493 --> 00:26:19.703
they'll need a full chest
of toys.

636
00:26:19.870 --> 00:26:22.039
Indigenous ambulance.
40.000 on the clock.

637
00:26:22.122 --> 00:26:25.417
full tank of laughing gas
and four brand new boots.

638
00:26:25.876 --> 00:26:27.836
Baker. door.
(door clanks open)

639
00:26:30.255 --> 00:26:31.673
Abracadabra.

640
00:26:31.757 --> 00:26:33.342
Say hello to Javier.

641
00:26:33.467 --> 00:26:35.844
-GROUP: Hello. Javier.
-Hola. chicos.

642
00:26:36.011 --> 00:26:38.764
He's been a very clever boy
and got the full shopping list.

643
00:26:39.014 --> 00:26:43.018
Two canoes. four oars.
two emergency outboards.

644
00:26:43.185 --> 00:26:47.564
Late 2010 Coche.
upgraded with an LS3 V8.

645
00:26:47.981 --> 00:26:50.234
Three KTM 450s.

646
00:26:50.317 --> 00:26:53.403
125 scooter for eggs
and fresh milk.

647
00:26:53.654 --> 00:26:58.283
Two Polaris Razors with 190hp
and plenty of torque.

648
00:26:59.201 --> 00:27:00.327
And Teddy for fishing.

649
00:27:00.744 --> 00:27:02.955
We've got a full set
of knives and forks.

650
00:27:03.247 --> 00:27:04.289
We've got your
reach out attachment

651
00:27:04.373 --> 00:27:05.582
for the long range slot.

652
00:27:05.791 --> 00:27:08.293
Noise makers. cloudies.
blinders.

653
00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:11.839
We've got 9mils and 45s
avec hush puppies.

654
00:27:12.256 --> 00:27:14.675
Gucci AR with a 203
grenade launcher.

655
00:27:15.050 --> 00:27:17.678
Brand new boom stick
with 40mil butt plugs.

656
00:27:18.011 --> 00:27:20.472
Top cigars for the Charlie Gs
for ground to air.

657
00:27:20.556 --> 00:27:21.765
And finally...

658
00:27:22.349 --> 00:27:25.102
24 ice cold cervezas.

659
00:27:25.727 --> 00:27:26.895
Please drink responsibly.

660
00:27:27.604 --> 00:27:28.897
BRONCO: Alright ladies.
don't get excited

661
00:27:28.981 --> 00:27:29.982
about our accommodation.

662
00:27:30.065 --> 00:27:31.150
It's not the Savoy.

663
00:27:31.567 --> 00:27:33.110
We're hidden in
the most remote part

664
00:27:33.193 --> 00:27:34.361
of Salazar's Island.

665
00:27:34.486 --> 00:27:36.780
We chose this safe house
due to its proximity

666
00:27:36.864 --> 00:27:40.576
to all three extraction points
and its historical tunnels.

667
00:27:40.784 --> 00:27:42.744
should we need to get
Rachel out discreetly.

668
00:27:42.870 --> 00:27:46.248
Rachel is only ever going to be
in one of two places.

669
00:27:46.582 --> 00:27:47.791
Either here at the villa.

670
00:27:48.208 --> 00:27:49.459
or at Salazar's hotel.

671
00:27:49.877 --> 00:27:52.087
He lives in the penthouse suite

672
00:27:52.171 --> 00:27:53.589
which is where they will meet.

673
00:27:53.881 --> 00:27:55.966
If things get exciting.

674
00:27:56.049 --> 00:27:57.009
we extract Mum.

675
00:27:57.217 --> 00:27:58.343
assess the threat level.

676
00:27:58.427 --> 00:27:59.595
bring her back to the villa

677
00:27:59.928 --> 00:28:01.138
and get her off the island.

678
00:28:01.346 --> 00:28:02.681
Three extraction points.

679
00:28:03.015 --> 00:28:04.725
BRONCO: If we need to move
Rachel from the hotel.

680
00:28:04.808 --> 00:28:06.476
we take the east evac route.

681
00:28:06.602 --> 00:28:09.354
We'll take the SUVs through the
town through the storm drains

682
00:28:09.438 --> 00:28:10.731
to two awaiting RIBs.

683
00:28:10.814 --> 00:28:12.441
If we need to extract her
from the villa.

684
00:28:12.524 --> 00:28:14.860
we go from an airfield
on the north of the island.

685
00:28:14.943 --> 00:28:16.528
Jets and helicopters are a no-go

686
00:28:16.612 --> 00:28:18.572
because Salazar controls
the skies.

687
00:28:18.655 --> 00:28:20.282
That's why we came here by boat.

688
00:28:20.532 --> 00:28:22.242
We have two gyrocopters waiting.

689
00:28:22.326 --> 00:28:23.327
They'll go undetected.

690
00:28:23.535 --> 00:28:25.787
The west evac
is our last resort.

691
00:28:25.871 --> 00:28:28.040
There's no other way
off the island.

692
00:28:28.415 --> 00:28:31.251
Each route has its own
challenges but we need to reach

693
00:28:31.335 --> 00:28:33.921
these points as quickly
and efficiently as possible.

694
00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:36.256
We're gonna be ready
for any eventuality

695
00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:37.799
and practice until
we get it right.

696
00:28:37.966 --> 00:28:41.386
But this is Salazar's Island.

697
00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:43.263
The police are on payroll

698
00:28:43.639 --> 00:28:46.808
and he has a reasonably
experienced private army.

699
00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:47.809
How many?

700
00:28:47.893 --> 00:28:48.894
Best guess. 50.

701
00:28:49.436 --> 00:28:51.897
-What's that all about?
-Considering his activities.

702
00:28:52.147 --> 00:28:54.608
he takes some comfort
from having a small militia.

703
00:28:54.733 --> 00:28:56.276
BRONCO: The police station
is an issue.

704
00:28:56.443 --> 00:28:57.986
If anyone ends up inside.
we need to know

705
00:28:58.070 --> 00:28:58.946
how to get 'em out.

706
00:28:59.029 --> 00:28:59.988
Where do you wanna start?

707
00:29:00.072 --> 00:29:01.573
Well. first we recce the routes

708
00:29:01.657 --> 00:29:03.909
and then we go look at the hotel
and the police station.

709
00:29:03.992 --> 00:29:04.993
We'll split up.

710
00:29:05.118 --> 00:29:06.161
Gucci. Dunne and Baker.

711
00:29:06.328 --> 00:29:07.829
you recce the north evac point

712
00:29:07.955 --> 00:29:09.706
and log a flight time
to the mainland.

713
00:29:09.831 --> 00:29:13.085
Bronco. Moreno and yours truly.

714
00:29:13.752 --> 00:29:16.213
We'll recce the fastest route
from Salazar's penthouse

715
00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:19.299
through the city
to the east evac point.

716
00:29:19.758 --> 00:29:21.593
(horns blaring)

717
00:29:22.719 --> 00:29:24.763
Hey. Captain Sensible.
can you. er.

718
00:29:24.972 --> 00:29:26.223
can you just slow down
a little bit.

719
00:29:26.306 --> 00:29:27.516
You're starting
to make me nervous.

720
00:29:29.768 --> 00:29:31.395
Time really does stand still...

721
00:29:32.312 --> 00:29:33.105
when I'm with you.

722
00:29:33.563 --> 00:29:34.690
Dunno what you're
so grumpy about.

723
00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:35.774
You planned the route.

724
00:29:36.024 --> 00:29:37.651
(engine humming)
(horns blaring)

725
00:29:38.902 --> 00:29:42.114
If we're not careful.
your dad's gonna blow our cover.

726
00:29:42.239 --> 00:29:43.949
(window squeaking)

727
00:29:44.574 --> 00:29:46.076
-Okay. Thank you.
-Okay.

728
00:29:47.077 --> 00:29:48.745
Tell your dad not
to spend it all at once.

729
00:29:49.079 --> 00:29:50.914
(motorbike revving)

730
00:29:51.331 --> 00:29:53.041
(motorbikes revving)

731
00:29:53.208 --> 00:29:54.710
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

732
00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:57.671
That two wheels
is better than four.

733
00:29:58.505 --> 00:30:00.257
BRONCO: Okay. sweethearts.
we'll run the full route

734
00:30:00.340 --> 00:30:01.633
to the east evacuation point.

735
00:30:01.717 --> 00:30:02.676
If we need to get her out.

736
00:30:02.759 --> 00:30:03.969
Mom will be transported

737
00:30:04.052 --> 00:30:05.304
on the back of the bike.

738
00:30:05.387 --> 00:30:06.972
(motorbike revving)

739
00:30:09.766 --> 00:30:10.851
(horn blaring)

740
00:30:11.059 --> 00:30:12.561
MORENO: We've got a police car
up ahead.

741
00:30:12.644 --> 00:30:13.687
BRONCO: Who wants to kick 'em
in the ass

742
00:30:13.770 --> 00:30:14.813
and see if they'll kick back?

743
00:30:15.022 --> 00:30:15.981
MORENO: Leave it with me.

744
00:30:16.064 --> 00:30:16.982
BRONCO: Good man. Moreno.

745
00:30:17.065 --> 00:30:18.317
Try not to end up in jail.

746
00:30:18.608 --> 00:30:20.485
(motorbike revving)

747
00:30:20.986 --> 00:30:23.113
(sirens blaring)
(shouting in Spanish)

748
00:30:23.613 --> 00:30:25.824
(motorbike revving)
(tyres screeching)

749
00:30:26.325 --> 00:30:27.576
BRONCO: Head to
the storm drains.

750
00:30:27.826 --> 00:30:29.202
See if they have
the stomach to follow.

751
00:30:29.286 --> 00:30:31.580
(shouting in Spanish)
(motorbike revving)

752
00:30:32.789 --> 00:30:34.082
MORENO: This is
too fuckin' easy.

753
00:30:35.083 --> 00:30:36.585
What I need is a pig on a bike.

754
00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:38.170
(sirens blaring)
(tyres screeching)

755
00:30:38.253 --> 00:30:39.838
(motorbike revving)

756
00:30:44.634 --> 00:30:46.470
SID: Moreno. what the fuck
are you doing?

757
00:30:46.553 --> 00:30:48.263
MORENO: You do your thing.
let me do mine.

758
00:30:49.765 --> 00:30:50.974
BRONCO: Looks like your
dream's come true.

759
00:30:51.058 --> 00:30:52.601
You've picked up a pig
on two wheels.

760
00:30:53.101 --> 00:30:54.227
MORENO: Yep. thank you!

761
00:30:55.187 --> 00:30:57.189
(motorbike revving)
(sirens blaring)

762
00:31:01.485 --> 00:31:04.112
You know. surprisingly he's not
completely shit. this guy.

763
00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:06.740
(motorbike revving)
(tyres screeching)

764
00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:09.451
MORENO: Let's see if this fucker
likes the idea

765
00:31:09.534 --> 00:31:11.036
of dropping twenty foot
into a storm drain.

766
00:31:11.119 --> 00:31:12.788
(motorbike revving)
(tyres screeching)

767
00:31:16.541 --> 00:31:18.126
(motorbike revving)

768
00:31:18.210 --> 00:31:19.544
(sirens blaring)

769
00:31:19.628 --> 00:31:20.796
(shouting in Spanish)

770
00:31:21.713 --> 00:31:22.672
(motorbike revving)

771
00:31:24.299 --> 00:31:25.717
MORENO: Sadly. he didn't follow.

772
00:31:25.801 --> 00:31:27.010
BRONCO: Coming in beside you.

773
00:31:33.141 --> 00:31:34.518
BRONCO: Turns out
you do actually

774
00:31:34.601 --> 00:31:35.852
have some talents. Moreno.

775
00:31:36.103 --> 00:31:37.229
(dramatic music)

776
00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:45.779
SID: Okay. Looks like that'll
work if we need it to.

777
00:31:45.904 --> 00:31:47.572
MORENO: So. a boat will
pick us up from here?

778
00:31:47.656 --> 00:31:48.698
SID: That's the idea.

779
00:31:49.116 --> 00:31:50.450
But the bikes won't work
if we need

780
00:31:50.534 --> 00:31:51.952
to take someone
who's incapacitated.

781
00:31:52.244 --> 00:31:53.870
For that. we'll need
the ambulance to get us

782
00:31:53.954 --> 00:31:56.456
through town and an ATV
to get us down the storm drain.

783
00:31:56.748 --> 00:31:58.125
Then we get them off on a RIB.

784
00:31:59.167 --> 00:32:00.877
BRONCO: Okay.
so onto the next route.

785
00:32:01.086 --> 00:32:02.671
North evac is a straight shot

786
00:32:02.754 --> 00:32:04.548
through a wind farm
outside the city.

787
00:32:04.631 --> 00:32:07.634
It is our primary extraction
point as our gyrocopters

788
00:32:07.717 --> 00:32:10.220
are the fastest way
to get Rachel off the island.

789
00:32:10.345 --> 00:32:12.681
We'll need to get these
operational and onto the runway

790
00:32:12.764 --> 00:32:14.266
in no more than three minutes.

791
00:32:14.766 --> 00:32:17.602
The only way to do that
is to rehearse.

792
00:32:17.769 --> 00:32:19.187
(blades whirring)

793
00:32:27.863 --> 00:32:28.822
(blades slowing)

794
00:32:29.906 --> 00:32:32.617
(sighs) It takes 25 minutes
to get to the mainland.

795
00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:34.411
Twenty five minutes?

796
00:32:34.661 --> 00:32:36.621
Give me something faster.
I'll get it there quicker.

797
00:32:36.788 --> 00:32:37.831
How long from the hotel?

798
00:32:37.956 --> 00:32:39.499
Cut it down to nine
and a half minutes.

799
00:32:39.666 --> 00:32:40.917
Get it down to eight and a half.

800
00:32:41.042 --> 00:32:42.252
That's not possible.

801
00:32:42.377 --> 00:32:44.087
You're right. six and a half
is possible.

802
00:32:44.171 --> 00:32:45.255
SID: This is how we're
gonna do it.

803
00:32:45.338 --> 00:32:46.465
We'll take Rachel
from the hotel.

804
00:32:46.548 --> 00:32:47.674
These have to be out of the shed

805
00:32:47.757 --> 00:32:49.092
and in the air in three minutes.

806
00:32:49.217 --> 00:32:51.928
You two pilot and take Rachel
and me with you.

807
00:32:52.095 --> 00:32:55.015
BRONCO: If this doesn't work.
we go to the west evac.

808
00:32:55.724 --> 00:32:57.017
That means back to the villa.

809
00:32:57.601 --> 00:32:58.518
through the tunnel.

810
00:32:58.894 --> 00:33:01.605
onto the bikes
until it's easier by foot.

811
00:33:01.938 --> 00:33:03.773
Then there's an obstacle.

812
00:33:03.899 --> 00:33:07.486
The upside of the obstacle
is no-one can follow us.

813
00:33:07.611 --> 00:33:10.697
But the downside of
the obstacle is. er...

814
00:33:12.616 --> 00:33:13.575
That's the straightest line?

815
00:33:14.993 --> 00:33:15.994
Fuck off.

816
00:33:17.120 --> 00:33:18.455
I foresee a problem.

817
00:33:18.705 --> 00:33:20.749
Point A. the villa is two
and a half miles that way.

818
00:33:20.832 --> 00:33:22.042
Point B. the west evac point

819
00:33:22.125 --> 00:33:23.793
is seven and a half miles
that way.

820
00:33:23.960 --> 00:33:25.337
This is the straightest line.

821
00:33:28.048 --> 00:33:30.383
Now. I am aware that
there is a 300 foot deep

822
00:33:30.467 --> 00:33:32.260
untraversable ravine before you.

823
00:33:33.512 --> 00:33:35.055
But fortunately.

824
00:33:35.388 --> 00:33:37.849
Baker and I have put a great
deal of thought into this.

825
00:33:38.141 --> 00:33:41.311
And we've discovered that if you
give yourself enough runway.

826
00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.396
build up some speed.

827
00:33:43.813 --> 00:33:45.440
and flap your arms like so...

828
00:33:45.857 --> 00:33:47.025
(suspenseful music)

829
00:33:50.070 --> 00:33:52.489
It should take the bump
out of the landing.

830
00:33:54.366 --> 00:33:57.744
Alternatively. there is another
option for the less adventurous.

831
00:33:57.827 --> 00:34:00.372
(button clicks)
(line whirring)

832
00:34:01.414 --> 00:34:03.416
(dramatic music)
It's. er. called a zipline.

833
00:34:03.667 --> 00:34:04.918
(line whirring)

834
00:34:07.546 --> 00:34:10.090
SID: The zipline takes us
to where our ATVs are hidden.

835
00:34:10.173 --> 00:34:11.466
(motor revving)

836
00:34:11.550 --> 00:34:12.342
BRONCO: Then there's the matter

837
00:34:12.425 --> 00:34:13.176
of getting to the harbour

838
00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:14.719
as quickly as possible.

839
00:34:15.178 --> 00:34:16.888
SID: And like with
the other routes.

840
00:34:17.305 --> 00:34:18.765
we'll need to time
and rehearse this too.

841
00:34:21.309 --> 00:34:22.352
Do it again!

842
00:34:26.231 --> 00:34:27.774
(engine revving)

843
00:34:33.071 --> 00:34:34.656
(motorbike revving)

844
00:34:35.782 --> 00:34:37.409
(tyres screeching)
(engine idling)

845
00:34:38.034 --> 00:34:40.120
-What happened there?
-I can do better.

846
00:34:40.203 --> 00:34:41.663
Go on. Fuck off.
(motorbike revving)

847
00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:43.999
-Vroom vroom.
-Jesus! Fuck!

848
00:34:44.749 --> 00:34:45.584
Board...

849
00:34:47.627 --> 00:34:48.628
Four minutes.

850
00:34:49.379 --> 00:34:50.714
(rifle fires)

851
00:34:51.881 --> 00:34:53.008
Four feet to the left.

852
00:34:53.383 --> 00:34:54.551
(rifle fires)

853
00:34:55.510 --> 00:34:56.636
MORENO: Three feet to the left.

854
00:34:56.761 --> 00:34:58.179
(chain rattling)

855
00:34:58.263 --> 00:34:59.848
(rifle fires)
Two feet to the left.

856
00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:01.182
(mine beeps)

857
00:35:04.102 --> 00:35:05.228
(rifle fires)

858
00:35:07.647 --> 00:35:08.523
Bingo.

859
00:35:11.943 --> 00:35:13.236
(engine revving)

860
00:35:14.154 --> 00:35:15.655
(motorbike revving)

861
00:35:17.365 --> 00:35:18.283
Do it again.

862
00:35:18.366 --> 00:35:19.200
(dramatic music)

863
00:35:21.119 --> 00:35:22.037
Four minutes.

864
00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:23.371
Not too shabby.

865
00:35:23.622 --> 00:35:24.414
Let's go again.

866
00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:26.958
(gunfire)
(motorbike revving)

867
00:35:27.459 --> 00:35:28.877
MORENO: Argh. dammit!

868
00:35:32.380 --> 00:35:33.965
2:59. Got it.

869
00:35:34.090 --> 00:35:35.800
Aaargh!
(blades whirring)

870
00:35:38.094 --> 00:35:40.138
Three. two. one...

871
00:35:40.472 --> 00:35:41.806
(gun firing)

872
00:35:45.602 --> 00:35:46.394
Not bad.

873
00:35:46.770 --> 00:35:48.063
(gunfire)
(motorbikes revving)

874
00:35:53.902 --> 00:35:55.862
In contingency. if the north
evac fails

875
00:35:55.945 --> 00:35:57.072
and we have pursuing vehicles.

876
00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:59.574
we lead them into a banana pie.

877
00:35:59.699 --> 00:36:01.910
There'll be one vehicle
and two bikes.

878
00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:04.788
Bikes will peel off and ram's
horn behind the pursuers.

879
00:36:04.913 --> 00:36:06.665
(motorbikes revving)

880
00:36:07.791 --> 00:36:09.334
You're gonna dig a hole
in the floor.

881
00:36:10.251 --> 00:36:11.127
Question.

882
00:36:11.211 --> 00:36:12.379
What are we digging with?

883
00:36:13.338 --> 00:36:14.297
With your finger.

884
00:36:15.048 --> 00:36:16.174
Or you could use an excavator.

885
00:36:16.299 --> 00:36:17.342
(engine chugging)

886
00:36:18.134 --> 00:36:20.720
BRONCO: You put the crank arm
twenty yards to the right.

887
00:36:20.929 --> 00:36:23.181
Dusty trap doors
to snag enemy traffic.

888
00:36:23.264 --> 00:36:24.015
(pickaxe smashes)

889
00:36:24.099 --> 00:36:25.016
(grunting)

890
00:36:25.225 --> 00:36:26.851
-Aargh...
-BRONCO: We drive over.

891
00:36:27.602 --> 00:36:29.020
I'll jump out and trigger.

892
00:36:29.437 --> 00:36:30.522
(thudding)

893
00:36:31.481 --> 00:36:32.857
We'll lose at least one
down the hole

894
00:36:32.941 --> 00:36:34.609
and then whatever's left.
I'll hose off

895
00:36:34.693 --> 00:36:36.069
with the help of the two bikes.

896
00:36:37.028 --> 00:36:38.988
I'll take Mum and continue
to the west evac.

897
00:36:39.531 --> 00:36:41.116
Did the picture
make things clear?

898
00:36:43.785 --> 00:36:45.036
GROUP: Crystal.

899
00:36:47.163 --> 00:36:48.873
The only time Rachel's
going to be vulnerable

900
00:36:48.957 --> 00:36:50.834
is in transit between the hotel
and the villa.

901
00:36:51.084 --> 00:36:52.919
If she insists on stopping
for ice cream.

902
00:36:53.128 --> 00:36:54.587
we will not be able
to stop her.

903
00:36:55.130 --> 00:36:56.840
So. Gucci. you get the drone up

904
00:36:57.048 --> 00:36:59.217
and everyone else.
invisible but useful.

905
00:36:59.718 --> 00:37:01.386
We do not want them knowing
about the full team

906
00:37:01.469 --> 00:37:02.679
and if they come for a bite.

907
00:37:02.804 --> 00:37:05.098
I want them to lose
their fucking teeth.

908
00:37:06.099 --> 00:37:07.642
We know the evac points.

909
00:37:07.851 --> 00:37:09.185
Speed is our priority.

910
00:37:09.269 --> 00:37:10.645
But because there's
three new routes.

911
00:37:10.729 --> 00:37:12.564
because it is unknown territory.

912
00:37:12.647 --> 00:37:14.107
because it is his island

913
00:37:14.190 --> 00:37:16.234
and because we are outnumbered
ten to one.

914
00:37:16.359 --> 00:37:17.986
we are going to keep rehearsing.

915
00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:19.237
And by rehearse.

916
00:37:19.320 --> 00:37:20.530
he means tick every box.

917
00:37:20.613 --> 00:37:21.656
(engine revving)

918
00:37:21.740 --> 00:37:22.574
Tick every tock.

919
00:37:22.657 --> 00:37:23.575
(motorbike revving)

920
00:37:23.658 --> 00:37:24.451
Lube every wheel.

921
00:37:24.534 --> 00:37:25.452
(brakes screeching)

922
00:37:25.577 --> 00:37:26.578
Lick every stamp.

923
00:37:27.454 --> 00:37:31.416
And steal every inch until
all of those routes are ours.

924
00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:34.919
SID: We need to be one step
ahead of Salazar.

925
00:37:35.003 --> 00:37:36.588
BRONCO: We need to know
his movements.

926
00:37:36.671 --> 00:37:38.590
We need to hear
his conversations.

927
00:37:38.673 --> 00:37:40.925
SID: We need ears
in the penthouse suite.

928
00:37:41.092 --> 00:37:42.761
BRONCO: We can only do this
before he knows

929
00:37:42.844 --> 00:37:44.137
that we're on his island.

930
00:37:44.596 --> 00:37:46.347
Dunne will check out
the access routes.

931
00:37:46.723 --> 00:37:49.476
SID: Moreno and Baker will recce
the hotel's rear exits.

932
00:37:49.726 --> 00:37:52.061
BRONCO: Sidney and I will
casually enter the lobby.

933
00:37:52.187 --> 00:37:53.563
SID: Bronco will have
a heart attack

934
00:37:53.646 --> 00:37:55.523
to distract the hotel manager.
(gasping)

935
00:37:56.107 --> 00:37:58.318
BRONCO: She will then kindly
donate her skeleton key.

936
00:37:58.985 --> 00:38:00.487
SID: Bronco will then recover.

937
00:38:00.612 --> 00:38:02.989
-And then Sid will inform her...
-It's low blood sugar.

938
00:38:03.156 --> 00:38:04.365
Just needs a sweetie.

939
00:38:04.449 --> 00:38:05.909
And then my husband and I
will make our way

940
00:38:05.992 --> 00:38:06.951
to the penthouse suite.

941
00:38:07.035 --> 00:38:08.703
Whilst Gucci cuts the cameras.

942
00:38:08.787 --> 00:38:09.871
GUCCI: Cameras are down.

943
00:38:12.165 --> 00:38:14.083
(suspenseful music)

944
00:38:18.087 --> 00:38:19.172
Cameras are off.

945
00:38:25.804 --> 00:38:26.930
(statue clunks)

946
00:38:28.181 --> 00:38:29.098
Shh.

947
00:38:29.641 --> 00:38:30.600
Hear no evil.

948
00:38:34.896 --> 00:38:35.688
Get it in.

949
00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:38.733
I think I know what I'm doing.

950
00:38:52.038 --> 00:38:52.872
Three exits.

951
00:38:53.540 --> 00:38:54.541
Door we came in.

952
00:38:54.624 --> 00:38:55.583
fire escape...

953
00:38:56.459 --> 00:38:58.253
Or over the edge
for a neck breaker.

954
00:38:58.670 --> 00:39:00.421
If anything relevant
is said there.

955
00:39:01.005 --> 00:39:02.674
or if Salazar loses
his patience.

956
00:39:02.757 --> 00:39:03.758
we should know about it

957
00:39:03.842 --> 00:39:05.718
and we get Rachel
off the island.

958
00:39:06.010 --> 00:39:08.680
If they open fire. we fire back
and we do not miss.

959
00:39:08.847 --> 00:39:11.474
If and when Salazar's police
force turn up.

960
00:39:11.766 --> 00:39:12.725
we make them pay.

961
00:39:14.060 --> 00:39:15.478
How exactly do you
wanna handle that?

962
00:39:15.562 --> 00:39:16.563
Oh. you're gonna handle that.

963
00:39:17.355 --> 00:39:19.524
You're gonna plant engine
killers under their cars.

964
00:39:25.363 --> 00:39:27.699
If anyone ends up
in that station.

965
00:39:27.991 --> 00:39:30.785
we need to know how to get them
out of that station.

966
00:39:31.578 --> 00:39:33.997
And if I recall correctly.
it's your turn to take the tour.

967
00:39:35.748 --> 00:39:37.375
(plaza chatter)

968
00:39:37.876 --> 00:39:38.877
Your boys are here.

969
00:39:41.004 --> 00:39:42.171
They look very athletic.

970
00:39:44.424 --> 00:39:45.633
It's only one night.

971
00:39:45.717 --> 00:39:47.760
Don't overdo it.
as you're prone to.

972
00:39:50.096 --> 00:39:51.139
And remember.

973
00:39:51.681 --> 00:39:52.599
I love you.

974
00:39:52.849 --> 00:39:54.684
('La Cucaracha' plays
in background)

975
00:39:57.103 --> 00:39:58.021
Wait for me.

976
00:40:00.398 --> 00:40:02.066
-One more thing...
-Shhh...

977
00:40:03.484 --> 00:40:04.777
Write it in a letter.

978
00:40:05.486 --> 00:40:06.404
But I don't write.

979
00:40:07.071 --> 00:40:08.406
No. not the sombrero.

980
00:40:10.700 --> 00:40:12.410
Oy-oy!

981
00:40:12.994 --> 00:40:13.995
Aah...

982
00:40:14.329 --> 00:40:16.205
La cucaracha ...

983
00:40:17.123 --> 00:40:18.708
SID: Little old me!

984
00:40:18.791 --> 00:40:21.044
(slurring) La cucaracha!
(phone ringing)

985
00:40:21.377 --> 00:40:22.921
La cucaracha ...

986
00:40:23.004 --> 00:40:25.006
-RACHEL: Are you ready?
-Yeah. we're ready.

987
00:40:25.214 --> 00:40:27.634
-Is it time?
-Yeah. you should get out here.

988
00:40:28.092 --> 00:40:29.969
Did you get me somewhere
nice to stay?

989
00:40:30.470 --> 00:40:31.846
Oh. it's a marble palace.

990
00:40:32.513 --> 00:40:35.183
Frette sheets and gold shitters.

991
00:40:35.558 --> 00:40:37.185
-Liar.
-Wherever you're gonna be

992
00:40:37.268 --> 00:40:39.103
sleeping in is a hell of a lot
more comfortable

993
00:40:39.187 --> 00:40:40.647
than where Sidney's gonna be
sleeping tonight.

994
00:40:40.730 --> 00:40:41.814
Yo! Hey!

995
00:40:41.898 --> 00:40:43.441
Right now. he's er. pissing

996
00:40:43.524 --> 00:40:44.984
on policeman's boots.

997
00:40:45.652 --> 00:40:47.111
Did you get what you need
from Wolfgang?

998
00:40:47.695 --> 00:40:48.821
It's coming.

999
00:40:49.322 --> 00:40:51.866
I just have one more thing
to do. I'll see you soon.

1000
00:40:52.158 --> 00:40:55.036
SID: La cucaracha...
You know it. ladies!

1001
00:40:55.119 --> 00:40:57.914
-La cucarach...
-Hey! Hey!

1002
00:40:58.706 --> 00:41:00.583
RACHEL: They're ready.
Let's get him to the island.

1003
00:41:02.418 --> 00:41:03.920
Let's make this personal.

1004
00:41:04.587 --> 00:41:05.588
Let's take his toys.

1005
00:41:06.714 --> 00:41:07.882
The jet and the boat.

1006
00:41:08.007 --> 00:41:09.801
He'll be flying to the island
on that jet.

1007
00:41:09.968 --> 00:41:12.679
Oh. he's a clever boy.
He'll find a way.

1008
00:41:13.137 --> 00:41:14.347
Let's go back to court.

1009
00:41:14.430 --> 00:41:16.808
The court approves seizure
of personal assets

1010
00:41:16.891 --> 00:41:19.018
belonging to Manuel Salazar.

1011
00:41:19.143 --> 00:41:20.770
Objection. Your Honor!

1012
00:41:20.853 --> 00:41:21.771
Overruled!

1013
00:41:22.689 --> 00:41:23.773
RACHEL: First. they'll
ground his plane

1014
00:41:23.856 --> 00:41:25.024
under international law.

1015
00:41:25.233 --> 00:41:29.320
Horowitz! I'm standing
outside my jet

1016
00:41:29.487 --> 00:41:33.157
and being told
it no longer belongs to me!

1017
00:41:33.324 --> 00:41:35.868
Y-yes. of-of course
it's your jet.

1018
00:41:35.952 --> 00:41:37.495
It's just a technical issue.

1019
00:41:37.578 --> 00:41:40.623
Why can't I fly?
It's my fucking jet!

1020
00:41:42.250 --> 00:41:44.669
It's been impounded
under international law.

1021
00:41:44.794 --> 00:41:48.756
Since when did I give a fuck
about international law?

1022
00:41:49.132 --> 00:41:51.509
And there's a-a little more.
You. you...

1023
00:41:51.926 --> 00:41:53.469
I think you might need
to brace yourself.

1024
00:41:53.553 --> 00:41:56.264
And then I'll impound
his boat under maritime law.

1025
00:41:56.347 --> 00:41:59.809
-He won't even let me on board.
-My boat! My fucking boat!

1026
00:41:59.892 --> 00:42:01.144
Now I'll have his attention.

1027
00:42:01.436 --> 00:42:03.187
You don't need to worry.
I am confident

1028
00:42:03.271 --> 00:42:06.315
that we will get them back...
in court.

1029
00:42:06.691 --> 00:42:08.109
SALAZAR: We are not
going to court.

1030
00:42:08.276 --> 00:42:09.944
I want to look her in the eye.

1031
00:42:11.946 --> 00:42:13.281
Set up a meeting on the island.

1032
00:42:16.784 --> 00:42:18.411
(door clanking)
Vamos.

1033
00:42:20.997 --> 00:42:22.790
(door creaks. clunks shut)

1034
00:42:24.834 --> 00:42:26.627
(clipboard clunks)
(background chatter)

1035
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:32.383
(handcuffs clunk)

1036
00:42:38.473 --> 00:42:39.766
(door rattles)

1037
00:42:44.562 --> 00:42:45.605
What took you so long?

1038
00:42:46.314 --> 00:42:48.608
I may have overdone it
when I pissed on his boots.

1039
00:42:49.150 --> 00:42:49.942
Got any news?

1040
00:42:52.904 --> 00:42:55.698
I. er...don't belong
to you anymore.

1041
00:42:56.574 --> 00:42:57.575
I don't care about that.

1042
00:42:57.909 --> 00:42:59.410
(suspenseful music)

1043
00:43:00.119 --> 00:43:00.870
Cameras?

1044
00:43:01.621 --> 00:43:03.498
They're connected
but they're unsophisticated.

1045
00:43:05.083 --> 00:43:05.917
Guards?

1046
00:43:06.375 --> 00:43:08.503
Give or take 12
and about 20 across the road.

1047
00:43:10.129 --> 00:43:11.839
-Guns?
-Yeah. Plenty.

1048
00:43:12.840 --> 00:43:13.841
Is there any way in the back?

1049
00:43:14.133 --> 00:43:15.968
Well. you gotta
blow a hole through the wall.

1050
00:43:17.595 --> 00:43:19.680
Next time. you're gonna spend
the night in the cell.

1051
00:43:20.765 --> 00:43:23.601
Nah. you're a soldier.
And you're good with the boys.

1052
00:43:23.768 --> 00:43:26.145
Yeah. you're right.
They'd eat you alive.

1053
00:43:26.604 --> 00:43:28.564
Ooh! On second thought...

1054
00:43:28.773 --> 00:43:30.566
(suspenseful music)
(engine starts)

1055
00:43:31.692 --> 00:43:33.444
I picked up their signal
on the way in.

1056
00:43:34.737 --> 00:43:35.696
Abracadabra.

1057
00:43:36.989 --> 00:43:38.991
You've got more tricks
than a clown's pocket

1058
00:43:39.826 --> 00:43:41.619
and you smell
like a wizard's sleeve.

1059
00:43:42.078 --> 00:43:43.955
(suspenseful music)

1060
00:43:45.998 --> 00:43:48.793
Here's our police station.
These are our cells.

1061
00:43:49.001 --> 00:43:50.378
We can't go in the cell wall

1062
00:43:50.461 --> 00:43:52.171
because it's surrounded
by another wall

1063
00:43:53.047 --> 00:43:54.382
and it's covered by cameras.

1064
00:43:54.632 --> 00:43:57.218
So. we have to go inside if we
want to get somebody outside.

1065
00:43:57.635 --> 00:43:58.970
We can go out the back wall.

1066
00:43:59.095 --> 00:44:00.805
It's got no cameras and we can
drive straight up to it.

1067
00:44:00.888 --> 00:44:02.223
-Ah.
-Drone's found

1068
00:44:02.306 --> 00:44:03.599
a nosy visitor. Sir.

1069
00:44:06.060 --> 00:44:08.437
Who do we have here?

1070
00:44:09.021 --> 00:44:11.149
Oh. ten points if you can guess.

1071
00:44:11.315 --> 00:44:13.067
-Okay. give me a clue.
-Big.

1072
00:44:13.276 --> 00:44:15.069
-Elephant.
-Bearded.

1073
00:44:16.821 --> 00:44:18.531
-Bearded elephant?
-Red.

1074
00:44:18.948 --> 00:44:20.158
Red bearded elephant?

1075
00:44:20.533 --> 00:44:23.077
Salazar's head of security.

1076
00:44:27.832 --> 00:44:29.000
Shall we go say hello?

1077
00:44:29.959 --> 00:44:32.003
Nah. I think you're doing
a good enough job.

1078
00:44:32.712 --> 00:44:35.256
SID: Phase three.
Conference with an enemy.

1079
00:44:35.840 --> 00:44:37.675
(dramatic music)

1080
00:44:40.344 --> 00:44:41.429
Majesty.

1081
00:44:41.846 --> 00:44:42.972
Captain Sensible.

1082
00:44:45.183 --> 00:44:46.809
(dramatic music)

1083
00:44:50.938 --> 00:44:52.064
Here. This is for you.

1084
00:44:53.774 --> 00:44:56.485
Oh...this isn't about
to get awkward. is it?

1085
00:44:56.569 --> 00:44:57.570
Just put it on.

1086
00:44:59.989 --> 00:45:01.115
(gasps)

1087
00:45:01.199 --> 00:45:04.911
Sidney... It's beautiful.
Thank you.

1088
00:45:04.994 --> 00:45:06.120
Is there anything in it?

1089
00:45:06.204 --> 00:45:07.288
There's a thing in the thing.

1090
00:45:07.747 --> 00:45:09.207
If you hold down the button.
no matter where you are

1091
00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:10.750
in the world. I'll find you.

1092
00:45:11.584 --> 00:45:13.836
RACHEL: I know when mistakes
are made. you need insurance.

1093
00:45:14.337 --> 00:45:15.922
Bronco and Sid are mine.

1094
00:45:16.005 --> 00:45:16.881
Eun Kon!

1095
00:45:17.465 --> 00:45:18.799
(bars rattling)

1096
00:45:19.467 --> 00:45:20.885
(cell door creaking)

1097
00:45:21.219 --> 00:45:23.429
With men like these.
you can't buy loyalty.

1098
00:45:24.096 --> 00:45:25.514
It must be earned.

1099
00:45:25.932 --> 00:45:27.767
Don't say a word. Follow me.

1100
00:45:28.017 --> 00:45:29.852
And I earned that
a hundred jobs ago

1101
00:45:29.936 --> 00:45:32.146
when I broke them out
of a prison in Chiang Mai.

1102
00:45:34.774 --> 00:45:36.442
-Are we being followed?
-Yep.

1103
00:45:40.947 --> 00:45:42.698
-Do we care?
-No.

1104
00:45:44.575 --> 00:45:46.535
Is there a reason
why we're driving so slow?

1105
00:45:46.661 --> 00:45:49.288
Dangerous things happen
to people who drive too fast.

1106
00:45:49.372 --> 00:45:51.165
And I wouldn't want them
to get in an accident.

1107
00:45:52.667 --> 00:45:54.418
(suspenseful music)
(engine revving)

1108
00:45:54.502 --> 00:45:55.795
(tyres screeching)

1109
00:46:08.015 --> 00:46:09.475
-Hello.
-Ma'am.

1110
00:46:12.311 --> 00:46:14.605
-Mr Beauregard.
-Sir.

1111
00:46:16.107 --> 00:46:20.236
So. marble palace.
Frette sheets. golden shitter?

1112
00:46:20.569 --> 00:46:22.113
Oh no. that's for the kids.

1113
00:46:22.697 --> 00:46:25.116
For you ma'am. we have 100%
electric RV.

1114
00:46:25.366 --> 00:46:27.410
organic sheets
and a compostable toilet.

1115
00:46:27.743 --> 00:46:28.828
Let me give you a tour.

1116
00:46:29.578 --> 00:46:30.288
Kids.

1117
00:46:31.372 --> 00:46:32.248
Ma'am.

1118
00:46:32.373 --> 00:46:34.125
(dramatic music)
(blades whirring)

1119
00:46:42.091 --> 00:46:43.718
(blades whirring)

1120
00:46:53.185 --> 00:46:54.687
(engines humming)

1121
00:46:56.856 --> 00:46:58.316
We start at 350.

1122
00:46:58.524 --> 00:47:00.276
Nudge it to four if we have to.

1123
00:47:00.818 --> 00:47:02.695
I need to start...(distortion)

1124
00:47:04.739 --> 00:47:06.324
RACHEL: Gucci. any news?

1125
00:47:06.532 --> 00:47:09.201
Ma'am. it sounds like
their final number is 400.

1126
00:47:09.618 --> 00:47:10.703
RACHEL: That's not gonna cut it.

1127
00:47:11.579 --> 00:47:13.247
(engine humming)

1128
00:47:17.084 --> 00:47:18.711
(dramatic music)

1129
00:47:33.059 --> 00:47:34.602
(suspenseful music)

1130
00:47:44.111 --> 00:47:45.863
Señor Salazar. Rachel Wild.

1131
00:47:48.574 --> 00:47:49.492
Miss Wild.

1132
00:47:50.743 --> 00:47:55.122
My client is prepared
to increase the previous offer.

1133
00:47:55.831 --> 00:47:57.583
Well. we're not losing
any time then.

1134
00:47:59.585 --> 00:48:04.298
Mr Salazar is offering
$350 million

1135
00:48:04.715 --> 00:48:06.300
to wrap this up today.

1136
00:48:06.842 --> 00:48:08.552
Well. I'm prepared
to be here till midnight

1137
00:48:08.636 --> 00:48:10.262
to find a way through
this challenge.

1138
00:48:10.763 --> 00:48:15.309
But. in the spirit of brevity.
throw a sharper dart.

1139
00:48:16.268 --> 00:48:17.144
Four hundred.

1140
00:48:18.562 --> 00:48:20.147
You won't get any more
than that.

1141
00:48:20.231 --> 00:48:21.690
Mr Salazar. we agreed
to stick to the...

1142
00:48:21.774 --> 00:48:23.442
-Shut up. Horowitz.
-Oh.

1143
00:48:24.151 --> 00:48:25.486
Well. the games begin.

1144
00:48:26.320 --> 00:48:29.073
We move from the tail
to the dog.

1145
00:48:29.824 --> 00:48:31.659
(suspenseful music)

1146
00:48:34.829 --> 00:48:38.040
You crossed the line.
Miss Wild. You play dirty.

1147
00:48:39.083 --> 00:48:42.920
For the first time in 15 years
I travelled to this meeting

1148
00:48:43.003 --> 00:48:44.880
in a jet that
didn't belong to me.

1149
00:48:47.842 --> 00:48:52.513
Why? Because someone didn't
respect the rules of the game.

1150
00:48:53.889 --> 00:48:55.641
Someone thought
they were clever.

1151
00:48:56.100 --> 00:48:58.811
But there is a line
separating business wealth

1152
00:48:58.894 --> 00:49:00.229
and personal assets.

1153
00:49:01.105 --> 00:49:03.399
Spencer Goldstein invested
in my business.

1154
00:49:04.191 --> 00:49:05.818
not in my personal space.

1155
00:49:07.194 --> 00:49:10.573
But you have marched an army
across that line.

1156
00:49:10.906 --> 00:49:12.992
Oh...wait.

1157
00:49:15.953 --> 00:49:16.996
I have an image.

1158
00:49:18.122 --> 00:49:20.666
Of a maiden in distress
clutching her pearls.

1159
00:49:20.749 --> 00:49:21.876
I too have an image.

1160
00:49:22.751 --> 00:49:25.671
But I would not be a gentleman
if I share it with you.

1161
00:49:26.046 --> 00:49:27.214
The debt is a billion dollars.

1162
00:49:27.298 --> 00:49:28.466
I'm just here to help you

1163
00:49:28.549 --> 00:49:29.967
facilitate in any way I can

1164
00:49:30.050 --> 00:49:32.011
you satisfying that obligation.

1165
00:49:32.303 --> 00:49:35.097
I am conscious of the small
print and I don't want you

1166
00:49:35.181 --> 00:49:38.184
to incur surcharges.
penalties. interest.

1167
00:49:39.852 --> 00:49:42.438
I'm also known to be
a rather effective nuisance.

1168
00:49:44.064 --> 00:49:45.691
Your blade has reached its hilt.

1169
00:49:46.525 --> 00:49:47.985
You can't cut any deeper.

1170
00:49:49.653 --> 00:49:51.447
Take what's on the table
and fuck off.

1171
00:49:51.739 --> 00:49:53.407
(dramatic music)

1172
00:50:03.209 --> 00:50:05.294
(suspenseful music)

1173
00:50:09.006 --> 00:50:11.300
RACHEL: Fuck...I need a drink.

1174
00:50:15.054 --> 00:50:16.305
(phone ringing)

1175
00:50:19.433 --> 00:50:20.893
-RACHEL: Glover?
-Boss.

1176
00:50:21.227 --> 00:50:23.854
I need more information.
I can't get him to budge.

1177
00:50:24.021 --> 00:50:26.065
We don't have the leverage
and he knows it.

1178
00:50:26.190 --> 00:50:29.443
GLOVER: (sighs) Look. unless
Wolfgang opens up more files.

1179
00:50:29.693 --> 00:50:30.778
we've bottomed out.

1180
00:50:33.405 --> 00:50:34.448
I want a beer.

1181
00:50:35.866 --> 00:50:36.784
SID: Understood.

1182
00:50:37.785 --> 00:50:39.286
We're making a quick pitstop.

1183
00:50:39.370 --> 00:50:41.330
-DUNNE: What are we doing?
-Boss wants a beer.

1184
00:50:41.455 --> 00:50:43.123
DUNNE: Hell of a time
for a fuckin' beer.

1185
00:50:43.624 --> 00:50:46.043
-Arrivederci. mon amour.
-Don't have too much fun.

1186
00:50:47.294 --> 00:50:48.420
(door shuts. opens)

1187
00:50:49.713 --> 00:50:51.549
SID: Mum and Bronco are heading
into the café.

1188
00:50:51.632 --> 00:50:54.134
Let's secure the perimeter.
Gucci. get the drone up.

1189
00:50:54.927 --> 00:50:56.053
MORENO: Just pulled up.

1190
00:50:58.389 --> 00:50:59.765
DUNNE: Are we all invited
for a beer?

1191
00:50:59.974 --> 00:51:02.309
-SID: Dunne. what's your ETA?
-I'm a minute out.

1192
00:51:02.476 --> 00:51:04.436
BRONCO: Reserved a table
in the back for us.

1193
00:51:04.853 --> 00:51:05.938
How romantic.

1194
00:51:06.772 --> 00:51:07.773
SID: Dunne. on your arrival.

1195
00:51:07.856 --> 00:51:09.358
cover the east side
of the square.

1196
00:51:09.441 --> 00:51:11.068
-Copy.
-Hm...

1197
00:51:12.736 --> 00:51:14.572
Gucci. how we looking?

1198
00:51:15.072 --> 00:51:15.990
Checking now.

1199
00:51:18.409 --> 00:51:20.202
A lot of movement
coming towards the café.

1200
00:51:20.744 --> 00:51:23.497
-Hola. What can I get you?
-Dos cervezas. por favor.

1201
00:51:23.581 --> 00:51:24.456
Perfect.

1202
00:51:25.749 --> 00:51:29.336
-How are we doing. Sid?
-Starting to smell a bit fishy.

1203
00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:33.257
DUNNE: See those two muppets
entering the café now?

1204
00:51:33.632 --> 00:51:34.883
They were at Salazar's hotel.

1205
00:51:36.135 --> 00:51:37.928
Bronco. two of Salazar's
guests joining you.

1206
00:51:39.138 --> 00:51:39.930
SID: Do you have them?

1207
00:51:41.932 --> 00:51:43.392
BRONCO: Yeah. got eyes on 'em.

1208
00:51:43.475 --> 00:51:45.477
(suspenseful music)

1209
00:51:46.186 --> 00:51:48.314
Well. this might be more complex
than I thought.

1210
00:51:48.564 --> 00:51:49.898
Well. you like complex.

1211
00:51:50.190 --> 00:51:51.442
GUCCI: Sid. there's two more
entering the bar.

1212
00:51:51.525 --> 00:51:52.401
Okay.

1213
00:51:53.068 --> 00:51:55.904
SID: Bronco. two new customers.
Side door. Bar area.

1214
00:51:56.030 --> 00:51:57.114
Do you have eyes on?

1215
00:51:58.282 --> 00:51:59.116
Eyes on.

1216
00:52:00.701 --> 00:52:02.578
GUCCI: Two more hostiles
outside the bar.

1217
00:52:02.786 --> 00:52:05.080
Bronco. it's getting congested.

1218
00:52:05.456 --> 00:52:07.416
-SID: Baker. you take the bar.
-Baker. you're on.

1219
00:52:07.499 --> 00:52:08.876
I'm bringing the car
to the rear of the café.

1220
00:52:08.959 --> 00:52:09.918
Right.

1221
00:52:10.002 --> 00:52:11.003
SID: Bronco. you're taking her

1222
00:52:11.086 --> 00:52:12.004
out the back door.

1223
00:52:13.047 --> 00:52:14.548
BAKER: Approaching bar entrance.

1224
00:52:14.882 --> 00:52:16.884
-Thank you.
-Just gonna borrow this.

1225
00:52:17.092 --> 00:52:18.636
(bar chatter)

1226
00:52:18.886 --> 00:52:19.845
(clears throat)

1227
00:52:21.305 --> 00:52:23.057
SID: Bronco.
how are we looking in there?

1228
00:52:23.891 --> 00:52:26.435
Yeah. we got two in the lobby.
we've got one in the back bar

1229
00:52:26.518 --> 00:52:27.728
and one in the corridor.

1230
00:52:28.479 --> 00:52:29.605
Do we have a problem?

1231
00:52:30.522 --> 00:52:33.233
Hm...more of a challenge
than a problem.

1232
00:52:34.526 --> 00:52:37.071
Hush puppies on.
we keep this quiet.

1233
00:52:37.279 --> 00:52:38.113
MORENO: Copy.

1234
00:52:39.198 --> 00:52:41.700
Mexico. you've got two bogies
coming from behind you.

1235
00:52:41.784 --> 00:52:42.826
MORENO: I'm on 'em.

1236
00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:45.162
-Eyes on. Guch?
-Two more incoming.

1237
00:52:45.329 --> 00:52:47.039
DUNNE: It's an entire fucking
football team.

1238
00:52:47.206 --> 00:52:49.166
Dunne. stand by.
(motorbike revving)

1239
00:52:49.249 --> 00:52:50.793
Anyone else's pants
getting tighter?

1240
00:52:50.876 --> 00:52:51.877
Gucci. sit rep?

1241
00:52:51.960 --> 00:52:53.087
Four sitting out front.

1242
00:52:53.170 --> 00:52:53.962
Four inside.

1243
00:52:55.089 --> 00:52:56.882
Sidney. the back door's
still clear.

1244
00:52:57.758 --> 00:53:00.219
SID: I'll leave the car running
at the back door.

1245
00:53:00.302 --> 00:53:01.804
Entering the rear
of the building.

1246
00:53:01.887 --> 00:53:03.639
GUCCI: Got an Escalade inbound.

1247
00:53:04.515 --> 00:53:06.266
BAKER: There's at least
six on board.

1248
00:53:06.350 --> 00:53:08.185
MORENO: By my count.
that's 14 unfriendlies.

1249
00:53:08.268 --> 00:53:09.269
BRONCO: You set out there?

1250
00:53:09.395 --> 00:53:10.562
Yep. ready when you are.

1251
00:53:12.731 --> 00:53:14.358
SID: They'll be going
for an extraction.

1252
00:53:14.441 --> 00:53:17.194
Moving to the kitchen entrance.
On your command. Bronco.

1253
00:53:18.070 --> 00:53:21.115
Alright. I'm gonna take
the two in the lobby.

1254
00:53:22.116 --> 00:53:23.826
BRONCO: Sid. you take
the back bar.

1255
00:53:24.535 --> 00:53:26.203
Baker. take the corridor.

1256
00:53:26.537 --> 00:53:28.163
(suspenseful music)

1257
00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:29.581
Weapons are free.

1258
00:53:29.915 --> 00:53:30.958
(gun clicks)

1259
00:53:36.505 --> 00:53:38.382
(suspenseful music)

1260
00:53:46.974 --> 00:53:48.600
(chair scrapes)
(silencer gunshots)

1261
00:53:48.684 --> 00:53:51.645
(screaming)
Two down. Lobby clear.

1262
00:53:51.729 --> 00:53:53.564
-SID: Kitchen clear.
-BAKER: Bar clear.

1263
00:53:54.440 --> 00:53:55.774
(screaming)
Let's go.

1264
00:53:56.567 --> 00:53:57.818
BRONCO: Gucci. are we good?

1265
00:53:58.068 --> 00:53:59.570
Bronco. back door's clear. Go.

1266
00:54:00.404 --> 00:54:01.655
GUCCI: They're exiting
the escalade.

1267
00:54:02.865 --> 00:54:04.658
DUNNE: Go out the rear.
(gunshots)

1268
00:54:06.577 --> 00:54:07.619
MORENO: Engaging front entrance.

1269
00:54:08.162 --> 00:54:09.830
(gunfire)
(screaming)

1270
00:54:09.913 --> 00:54:11.248
BAKER: Get down!
(gunfire)

1271
00:54:11.331 --> 00:54:13.292
SID: Escalade. clear. Baker?

1272
00:54:13.542 --> 00:54:14.710
(gunfire)

1273
00:54:15.586 --> 00:54:16.378
BAKER: Clear.

1274
00:54:18.505 --> 00:54:19.590
BRONCO: Extracting Mom now.

1275
00:54:20.132 --> 00:54:21.341
(screaming. panicking)

1276
00:54:22.259 --> 00:54:23.761
SID: Good shooting.
Let's pack this up.

1277
00:54:24.219 --> 00:54:25.971
(shouting. panicking)

1278
00:54:26.180 --> 00:54:28.182
(dramatic music)

1279
00:54:29.391 --> 00:54:31.518
GUCCI: Bronco. you've got two
on a scooter.

1280
00:54:31.685 --> 00:54:33.353
(scooter revving)

1281
00:54:33.437 --> 00:54:35.314
(gunshots)
(crashing)

1282
00:54:35.898 --> 00:54:37.107
(gunshots)

1283
00:54:37.191 --> 00:54:38.609
-Bronco's clear.
-Let's go.

1284
00:54:40.861 --> 00:54:41.945
Get in. Lay down.

1285
00:54:42.029 --> 00:54:43.697
(dramatic music)

1286
00:54:43.864 --> 00:54:45.699
SID: Gucci. let's get
out of here.

1287
00:54:45.866 --> 00:54:46.909
GUCCI: Pulling up.

1288
00:54:50.287 --> 00:54:51.663
Bronco. we good?

1289
00:54:52.122 --> 00:54:54.541
We're good. Mom's secure.
Rendezvous at the villa.

1290
00:54:54.625 --> 00:54:56.001
(engine revving)

1291
00:54:56.418 --> 00:54:57.836
SID: Gucci. back to the villa.

1292
00:54:57.920 --> 00:55:00.005
No wheelspins. no speeding.
don't run any red lights.

1293
00:55:00.339 --> 00:55:02.591
Dunne. if anyone tries to stop
you. shoot them in the face.

1294
00:55:03.008 --> 00:55:05.385
(engines revving)

1295
00:55:07.846 --> 00:55:09.223
(Olssen exhales)

1296
00:55:09.431 --> 00:55:11.308
(suspenseful music)

1297
00:55:14.603 --> 00:55:15.813
It didn't work.

1298
00:55:17.439 --> 00:55:19.483
W-what didn't work?

1299
00:55:20.275 --> 00:55:21.360
Fourteen men.

1300
00:55:22.528 --> 00:55:24.738
-Fourteen men?
-Fourteen.

1301
00:55:24.988 --> 00:55:26.406
What do you mean.
'fourteen men'?

1302
00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.411
Don't tell me you've fallen
into her trap.

1303
00:55:31.787 --> 00:55:33.789
(suspenseful music)

1304
00:55:34.665 --> 00:55:36.375
HOROWITZ: If you tried
to kill her.

1305
00:55:36.458 --> 00:55:38.502
she'll get an emergency
injunction.

1306
00:55:40.128 --> 00:55:42.339
That will turn us upside down.

1307
00:55:44.716 --> 00:55:47.678
Legally. they'll be able
to see everything.

1308
00:55:49.221 --> 00:55:51.223
Get Wolfgang on the phone. now.

1309
00:55:53.016 --> 00:55:54.476
(phone vibrating)

1310
00:55:57.896 --> 00:55:59.481
(phone vibrating)

1311
00:56:05.487 --> 00:56:06.405
GLOVER: Boss?

1312
00:56:06.864 --> 00:56:08.407
Glover. talk to me.

1313
00:56:08.866 --> 00:56:11.869
Wolfgang's moving assets.
Big assets.

1314
00:56:12.452 --> 00:56:13.370
GLOVER: They're panicking.

1315
00:56:14.037 --> 00:56:16.123
(dramatic music)

1316
00:56:16.498 --> 00:56:17.749
I think we've got him.

1317
00:56:18.500 --> 00:56:20.752
Glover. I fucking love you.

1318
00:56:21.253 --> 00:56:23.505
Listen to me. this is what
you're gonna do.

1319
00:56:24.715 --> 00:56:27.050
Connect the assets
to his hidden businesses.

1320
00:56:27.217 --> 00:56:29.428
Attach them to his name
and shut them down.

1321
00:56:29.720 --> 00:56:31.847
We can crack the code
and read the cipher.

1322
00:56:32.306 --> 00:56:34.683
If we cut off his income
streams. he'll have no choice

1323
00:56:34.766 --> 00:56:37.394
but to come back to the table
and pay the full billion.

1324
00:56:37.686 --> 00:56:39.813
If you're all in. we're all in.

1325
00:56:41.106 --> 00:56:43.400
But if you want out.
we can get you out.

1326
00:56:44.109 --> 00:56:45.027
Right now.

1327
00:56:46.361 --> 00:56:47.362
We're staying.

1328
00:56:47.821 --> 00:56:49.990
Sidney. the gift you
gave Wolfgang

1329
00:56:50.073 --> 00:56:51.658
is the gift that kept on giving.

1330
00:56:51.825 --> 00:56:54.369
What started with a drip
ended in a deluge.

1331
00:56:54.703 --> 00:56:58.123
Now I know what Salazar's got
and where he's hiding it.

1332
00:56:58.582 --> 00:57:02.836
And my lawyers are gonna freeze.
seize and bleed him dry.

1333
00:57:03.045 --> 00:57:05.213
The court approves
the application to seek

1334
00:57:05.297 --> 00:57:07.507
international attachment orders.
(gavel bangs)

1335
00:57:07.591 --> 00:57:09.176
RACHEL: He'll be fucked.

1336
00:57:09.259 --> 00:57:12.262
Next. Skyecill.
chemical manufacturing.

1337
00:57:12.512 --> 00:57:14.514
Turnover $1.1 billion.

1338
00:57:14.723 --> 00:57:17.351
Look at the evidence.
Mr Horowitz. It's unambiguous.

1339
00:57:17.517 --> 00:57:19.436
The court approves
the application to seek

1340
00:57:19.519 --> 00:57:22.272
international attachment orders.
(gavel bangs)

1341
00:57:27.527 --> 00:57:29.029
RACHEL: The panic will set in.

1342
00:57:29.571 --> 00:57:32.074
Primostar Telecom.
His first company.

1343
00:57:32.491 --> 00:57:35.953
$800 million in assets.
His walls will close in.

1344
00:57:36.036 --> 00:57:38.372
A worldwide freezing order
will be put in place

1345
00:57:38.455 --> 00:57:39.456
with immediate effect.

1346
00:57:39.539 --> 00:57:40.832
Objection. Your Honour.

1347
00:57:40.916 --> 00:57:42.542
Denied. Motion is granted.

1348
00:57:43.502 --> 00:57:45.212
By now. they'll know
there's a leak.

1349
00:57:45.462 --> 00:57:48.757
I repeat. the motion to lift
the corporate veil is granted.

1350
00:57:49.466 --> 00:57:52.010
And finally. Arkon Digital
start-up.

1351
00:57:52.135 --> 00:57:54.554
Cash reserve of $385 million.

1352
00:57:54.721 --> 00:57:56.515
Freeze...
(dramatic music)

1353
00:57:56.765 --> 00:57:58.475
fuck...
(arguing)

1354
00:57:58.558 --> 00:58:00.435
...and seize.
(padlock clanks)

1355
00:58:00.560 --> 00:58:03.355
The motion to lift the corporate
veil is granted.

1356
00:58:03.438 --> 00:58:04.523
-Objection!
-Denied.

1357
00:58:04.606 --> 00:58:05.941
-Objection. Your Honour!
-Denied!

1358
00:58:07.150 --> 00:58:08.860
RACHEL: It was only a question
of time before they found

1359
00:58:08.944 --> 00:58:09.778
the Trojan rat.

1360
00:58:10.112 --> 00:58:11.154
But by now.

1361
00:58:11.238 --> 00:58:12.489
we have everything I need.

1362
00:58:12.614 --> 00:58:14.032
You have no idea how much this

1363
00:58:14.116 --> 00:58:16.326
is going to cost both of us.

1364
00:58:17.035 --> 00:58:19.204
(suspenseful music)

1365
00:58:29.047 --> 00:58:30.549
(phone ringing)

1366
00:58:33.218 --> 00:58:35.721
Horowitz. What do you want?

1367
00:58:36.388 --> 00:58:38.098
My client would like to see you.

1368
00:58:38.181 --> 00:58:38.974
Now.

1369
00:58:39.683 --> 00:58:41.351
What. now. now?

1370
00:58:41.643 --> 00:58:44.813
Yes. now. now.
That means...now.

1371
00:58:45.981 --> 00:58:47.315
I'll be there when I'm ready.

1372
00:58:49.985 --> 00:58:52.195
(suspenseful music)

1373
00:58:55.782 --> 00:58:57.242
Back into the lion's den.

1374
00:58:58.368 --> 00:59:00.287
Well. thanks to you
there's less lions.

1375
00:59:06.543 --> 00:59:07.836
(footsteps)

1376
00:59:09.463 --> 00:59:13.300
Miss Wild. I hear there
was a regrettable incident.

1377
00:59:13.425 --> 00:59:15.343
Well. regrettable for some.

1378
00:59:15.510 --> 00:59:17.721
As I'm sure Horowitz
has explained to you.

1379
00:59:18.096 --> 00:59:19.264
Once you try to kill me.

1380
00:59:19.347 --> 00:59:20.640
you've crossed a legal rubicon

1381
00:59:20.724 --> 00:59:22.017
you can't come back from.

1382
00:59:22.309 --> 00:59:24.519
Now. unless you want me to choke
off the oxygen

1383
00:59:24.603 --> 00:59:28.106
to any more of the ancillary
appendages you possess.

1384
00:59:28.482 --> 00:59:30.692
you'll pay the full ticket
and you'll pay it today.

1385
00:59:32.235 --> 00:59:33.820
You can have 800.

1386
00:59:34.529 --> 00:59:35.947
What the fuck?
I don't want eight.

1387
00:59:36.031 --> 00:59:37.657
I want the full fucking yard!

1388
00:59:37.741 --> 00:59:39.367
And I want my boat
and my jet back.

1389
00:59:39.451 --> 00:59:41.328
Ooh. a billionaire
without his toys.

1390
00:59:41.411 --> 00:59:44.706
An embarrassing paradox!
Get the fuck over it!

1391
00:59:51.338 --> 00:59:54.257
Know when you've won.
Miss Wild. Take the deal.

1392
00:59:54.341 --> 00:59:58.136
No! The deal is you pay
a billion dollars.

1393
00:59:58.220 --> 01:00:01.014
For all your chest banging.
have you recovered

1394
01:00:01.181 --> 01:00:02.808
even a single penny
of the debt?

1395
01:00:03.350 --> 01:00:04.184
No.

1396
01:00:05.268 --> 01:00:07.813
You'll accept the deal.
take the 800

1397
01:00:08.021 --> 01:00:09.523
and return my possessions.

1398
01:00:09.606 --> 01:00:11.691
You know I've seen
behind the curtain.

1399
01:00:11.942 --> 01:00:13.443
You have no more secrets.

1400
01:00:14.486 --> 01:00:17.239
Do you really want me
to resurrect all the bodies

1401
01:00:17.322 --> 01:00:18.281
you've been hiding?

1402
01:00:18.740 --> 01:00:21.368
Because I will let slip
the dogs of administrative war

1403
01:00:21.451 --> 01:00:24.412
and I'll share the exact
location of all those corpses

1404
01:00:24.496 --> 01:00:27.666
with every single investor
you've burned previously.

1405
01:00:30.168 --> 01:00:31.878
And it won't be me coming
for a billion.

1406
01:00:32.254 --> 01:00:33.797
It'll be them coming for five.

1407
01:00:34.589 --> 01:00:36.466
(suspenseful music)

1408
01:00:45.892 --> 01:00:46.852
The billion.

1409
01:00:48.353 --> 01:00:49.938
And you give everything back.

1410
01:00:51.648 --> 01:00:52.566
We're done here.

1411
01:00:52.899 --> 01:00:54.234
(footsteps)

1412
01:01:00.991 --> 01:01:01.950
Pay the bitch.

1413
01:01:04.494 --> 01:01:07.372
Your job was to make sure
nothing like this could happen.

1414
01:01:07.789 --> 01:01:09.416
(ominous music)

1415
01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:12.210
I'm letting you go. William.

1416
01:01:12.836 --> 01:01:14.629
Olsson will take you
to the airport.

1417
01:01:16.715 --> 01:01:18.592
(sinister music)

1418
01:01:18.758 --> 01:01:20.468
(sirens blaring)

1419
01:01:21.303 --> 01:01:22.929
(phone ringing)

1420
01:01:24.431 --> 01:01:26.183
Rachel. How can I help?

1421
01:01:26.433 --> 01:01:27.309
It's done.

1422
01:01:27.517 --> 01:01:28.310
What exactly?

1423
01:01:28.685 --> 01:01:30.687
Salazar's agreed to pay
the full amount.

1424
01:01:32.272 --> 01:01:33.857
That's exactly
what Braxton said.

1425
01:01:34.024 --> 01:01:35.901
Now. there's only two reasons

1426
01:01:35.984 --> 01:01:37.694
why that little red phone
could ring.

1427
01:01:37.777 --> 01:01:39.112
One. you're being fired.

1428
01:01:39.279 --> 01:01:41.406
Two. you're being congratulated
for the brilliant agent

1429
01:01:41.489 --> 01:01:44.326
you hired to help you recoup
your unrecoupable debt.

1430
01:01:45.535 --> 01:01:48.622
If it does. Rachel.
I will be very impressed.

1431
01:01:48.705 --> 01:01:51.666
No. when it does. you'll return
everything we seized.

1432
01:01:51.791 --> 01:01:53.919
Contractually that includes
the jet and the boat.

1433
01:01:54.127 --> 01:01:58.381
-Am I clear?
-Crystal. Consider it done.

1434
01:01:58.924 --> 01:02:03.678
Now. keep looking even harder
at the phone you're looking at.

1435
01:02:05.180 --> 01:02:07.474
Ring. ring.
Mazel-tov motherfucker.

1436
01:02:11.186 --> 01:02:12.145
(phone snaps shut)

1437
01:02:16.733 --> 01:02:18.443
So...as I was saying...

1438
01:02:18.526 --> 01:02:19.861
(phone ringing)

1439
01:02:21.238 --> 01:02:23.490
-Bobby.
-Mr Goldstein.

1440
01:02:25.283 --> 01:02:26.409
Congratulations.

1441
01:02:27.702 --> 01:02:28.828
(phone clicks)

1442
01:02:29.246 --> 01:02:31.164
(suspenseful music)

1443
01:02:36.670 --> 01:02:38.296
Bobby. are we really going
to fall out

1444
01:02:38.380 --> 01:02:40.090
over a hundred million?
Call me back.

1445
01:02:40.590 --> 01:02:41.925
(dial tone)

1446
01:02:43.260 --> 01:02:45.929
Getting money out of Salazar
was a stimulating game of chess

1447
01:02:46.012 --> 01:02:47.973
compared to dealing
with Spencer Goldstein.

1448
01:02:48.556 --> 01:02:50.225
You always said
they could never be trusted.

1449
01:02:53.770 --> 01:02:55.272
(water pouring)

1450
01:02:58.191 --> 01:03:00.277
(ominous music)

1451
01:03:00.694 --> 01:03:01.653
Who's that?

1452
01:03:02.195 --> 01:03:03.905
We're a thousand miles
from anywhere.

1453
01:03:05.073 --> 01:03:06.616
-Are we expecting anyone?
-No.

1454
01:03:07.284 --> 01:03:08.201
Rashid?

1455
01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:10.829
Rashid!

1456
01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:12.872
(ominous music)

1457
01:03:13.665 --> 01:03:15.667
Wait there. Rashid?

1458
01:03:21.715 --> 01:03:22.632
Rashid...

1459
01:03:24.092 --> 01:03:26.011
(suspenseful music)

1460
01:03:33.018 --> 01:03:34.978
(dramatic music)

1461
01:03:38.815 --> 01:03:39.691
Shereen!

1462
01:03:43.695 --> 01:03:44.571
Shereen!

1463
01:03:49.617 --> 01:03:50.452
Shereen!

1464
01:04:06.426 --> 01:04:08.136
(wind gusting)

1465
01:04:15.602 --> 01:04:17.479
(engine humming)

1466
01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:18.855
Hello. my lovely.

1467
01:04:22.650 --> 01:04:24.319
(watch ticking)

1468
01:04:24.944 --> 01:04:26.863
(dramatic music)

1469
01:04:48.885 --> 01:04:50.970
(sirens blaring)

1470
01:04:53.139 --> 01:04:55.141
(music playing faintly)

1471
01:04:55.350 --> 01:04:57.268
(treadmill whirring)

1472
01:04:57.644 --> 01:04:59.354
(footsteps)

1473
01:04:59.813 --> 01:05:01.481
(treadmill whirring)

1474
01:05:05.902 --> 01:05:06.986
(fumbling)

1475
01:05:08.029 --> 01:05:08.863
Who the fuck are you?

1476
01:05:09.197 --> 01:05:10.698
(Bobby gasping)
(treadmill beeps)

1477
01:05:12.534 --> 01:05:13.993
You can't just walk
into my office!

1478
01:05:14.786 --> 01:05:15.787
Oh yes. we can.

1479
01:05:16.121 --> 01:05:17.497
I've got security cameras.

1480
01:05:18.289 --> 01:05:19.290
There are people watching.

1481
01:05:20.083 --> 01:05:20.959
No. there aren't.

1482
01:05:21.292 --> 01:05:22.710
(Bobby gasping)

1483
01:05:23.086 --> 01:05:24.087
So. who are you?

1484
01:05:26.256 --> 01:05:27.090
What do you want?

1485
01:05:28.716 --> 01:05:30.051
Salazar's taken Rachel.

1486
01:05:31.553 --> 01:05:34.264
Oh...alright.

1487
01:05:35.640 --> 01:05:38.268
You're her boys. I see.
Well. that's kind of sweet.

1488
01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:41.396
It's being handled.

1489
01:05:41.980 --> 01:05:43.189
Everything's being handled.

1490
01:05:44.357 --> 01:05:46.734
How...exactly?

1491
01:05:48.653 --> 01:05:49.946
We're dealing with the Ministry
of Foreign Affairs.

1492
01:05:50.029 --> 01:05:51.156
we're talking to the State
Department.

1493
01:05:51.239 --> 01:05:52.490
we're dealing with
the Spanish police.

1494
01:05:52.574 --> 01:05:54.617
It's a...it's a highly complex

1495
01:05:54.701 --> 01:05:56.035
and evolving situation.

1496
01:05:56.244 --> 01:05:57.162
So. you're doing nothing.

1497
01:05:58.204 --> 01:06:01.291
Look. we all just
have to be patient

1498
01:06:01.374 --> 01:06:03.168
and Salazar will
get his toys back.

1499
01:06:03.251 --> 01:06:05.003
Rachel gets released.
She gets paid...

1500
01:06:05.253 --> 01:06:06.463
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.

1501
01:06:06.921 --> 01:06:08.465
(suspenseful music)

1502
01:06:10.049 --> 01:06:12.510
So. you're telling me that she
got you your money back

1503
01:06:12.594 --> 01:06:13.970
and she still
hasn't been paid?

1504
01:06:14.471 --> 01:06:15.680
That's not very nice.

1505
01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:18.600
Look. you stick to the dancing

1506
01:06:19.392 --> 01:06:20.560
and I'll do the thinking.

1507
01:06:20.810 --> 01:06:21.811
Don't be cute.

1508
01:06:22.937 --> 01:06:24.647
Nothing is as simple
as it seems.

1509
01:06:25.440 --> 01:06:26.357
Yes. it is.

1510
01:06:26.649 --> 01:06:28.234
(suspenseful music)

1511
01:06:28.568 --> 01:06:29.486
Pay your debts.

1512
01:06:39.662 --> 01:06:40.955
(door slams)

1513
01:06:48.296 --> 01:06:49.923
(footsteps)

1514
01:06:58.056 --> 01:07:02.185
Miss Wild. we made an agreement.

1515
01:07:02.852 --> 01:07:04.270
I kept my side.

1516
01:07:04.938 --> 01:07:06.564
Spencer Goldstein have not.

1517
01:07:06.773 --> 01:07:08.233
No. it's not that simple.

1518
01:07:09.359 --> 01:07:11.110
They have something
really valuable to me.

1519
01:07:11.736 --> 01:07:13.613
Now I have something
valuable to them.

1520
01:07:15.323 --> 01:07:17.742
No. you...you don't.

1521
01:07:18.493 --> 01:07:21.037
Even if they knew that I'm here.
well. they wouldn't care.

1522
01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:22.288
It won't register.

1523
01:07:22.664 --> 01:07:24.666
I'm worth less to them
than a stray dog.

1524
01:07:25.959 --> 01:07:28.294
Quite brilliantly.
you're worth billions.

1525
01:07:29.254 --> 01:07:30.713
But they manage trillions.

1526
01:07:30.964 --> 01:07:33.258
If they owned New York City.
you'd just be a...

